<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toramana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toramana was a ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huna-people">Hunas</a>, or Alchon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a>, who invaded north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> around the late fifth and early sixth centuries CE. By around 500 CE the Hunas under Toramana and then his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihirakula">Mihirakula</a> occupied large parts of north-western India. These invasions contributed significantly to the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toramana.jpg" alt="Toramana" width="235" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toramana_portrait_and_initials_Tora.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
